# Code Style Consistency (Awesome-adapted · gated)

Use when touching **3+ files** or doing refactor/rename — not for single-line fixes.

## Quick profile (read before writing)
1. Sample 2–3 neighbor files in the same web part folder
2. Note: naming (`handle*`, `I*` interfaces, `*Service`, `*WebPart`)
3. Note: import order (SPFx externals → shared → local)
4. Note: error handling style (throw vs return undefined vs log+graceful degrade)
5. Prefer **recent** files as style anchor

## Apply
- Match indentation, quote style, and brace layout of the folder
- Match test style in adjacent `*.test.ts` when adding tests
- Do not "normalize" unrelated legacy style in the same PR

## Defer to higher rules
- Security → `security-appsec`
- Minimal scope → `anti-overengineering`
- TS/React specifics → `typescript-code-quality` / `react-component-gated`

## Reject
- Mass reformat drives unrelated to user task
- Introducing Prettier/ESLint config changes without ask
